{
 "id": "GtaPhysicsC01",
 "slug": "gta-physics/c01",
 "chapter": "Cold open",
 "topic": "What if GTA6 physics were real?",
 "script": [
  {
   "beat": "p1",
   "text": "You trip on the top step at school. Normally, that's a very bad day. Today, you bounce."
  },
  {
   "beat": "p2",
   "text": "Down all twelve steps, like a rubber doll. And at the bottom, you just stand up."
  },
  {
   "beat": "p3",
   "text": "At the crosswalk, a delivery van bumps you at walking speed. You fly thirty feet, spin twice in the air, and land on your feet. The driver doesn't even stop."
  },
  {
   "beat": "p4",
   "text": "Your best friend Mo dares you to jump off his garage roof. So you do. You roll once, dust off your hoodie, and walk away."
  },
  {
   "beat": "p5",
   "text": "And floating over your head, there's something new. A little green bar. It shrinks a bit every time you land."
  },
  {
   "beat": "p6",
   "text": "Today, you run on video game physics."
  },
  {
   "beat": "p7",
   "text": "But what would all of this really do to a human body? And what happens when that little bar runs out?"
  }
 ],
